From: Julien Pivotto <291750+roidelapluie@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:19:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] tsdb: keep a single float chunk encoding option

tsdb.Options had both FloatChunkEncoding and ChunkEncodingFloats, which is the
same option twice. Resolve the chunk_encoding.floats config value into
FloatChunkEncoding in cmd/prometheus instead, and inline the resolution in
ApplyConfig.

The TSDB errors no longer name Prometheus config paths, so they read correctly
for downstream consumers.

Note: removing chunk_encoding.floats from the config file and reloading now
falls back to the encoding resolved at startup, not to the flag-derived default.

Signed-off-by: Julien Pivotto <291750+roidelapluie@users.noreply.github.com>
